# Kiril Stoyanovich comes home to answer Emil's challenge (docs/voice/kiril_stoyanovich.md). THE CHOICE of the
# region: stand with Emil (pack_challenge, Emil fights beside the party), stand aside or hand Emil back (Kiril leads),
# or turn on both (den_reckoning). `after` is Kiril ruling the den, if the party let him.

~ challenge
Narrator: Kiril comes up the passage from the cave mouth without hurrying: a huge, bare-chested man with a wolf pelt worn like a cloak and a grin full of long teeth. Behind him, in the dark, eyes. A great many eyes.
Kiril [smile]: Emil! Out of your jewellery. And you've made friends. Meat with swords. The master's guests, if I'm not mistaken.
Emil: I howled the challenge, Kiril. By the old law, you answer it.
Kiril: The old law kept us thin and hiding in the rocks. The new law eats.
Kiril: Here's the new law, guests. Stand aside, and you walk out of my hills alive. The master likes his guests unchewed. I'd hate to disappoint him.
if guest:ireena
Kiril [smile]: And the master's red-haired lady, in my den. Oh, he'll want to hear about this. He'll want to hear about it from me.
Ireena [angry]: Then tell him I said no. He's heard it before.
endif
if guest:ezmerelda
Kiril [smile]: And the Vistani huntress. How's the leg? I kept the boot. It's on my wall.
Ezmerelda: Then I'll come and fetch it, dog.
endif
-> choice

~ choice
* We stand with Emil. -> stand
* [if not flag.kiril_children_asked] And the children? -> children_q
* This is pack business. Settle it between the two of you. -> aside
* Take him back, Kiril. We want no quarrel with you. -> betray
* Neither of you leads anything. This den ends tonight. -> neither

~ children_q
set kiril_children_asked
Kiril: The pups? They're pack now, or they will be after the moon. Don't fret. I'll raise them right. Strong and hungry, like me.
interject tag:devout: Children aren't yours to raise, wolf.
Kiril: Everything in these hills is mine to raise. Ask the deer.
-> choice

~ stand
set pack_challenge_begun
Emil: Then stand close, and don't let them get behind you.
Kiril: Pity. You'd have made good company at the master's table. As the dinner.
interject class:wizard: Everyone stand somewhere I can see you. I'm about to be very loud.
combat pack_challenge

~ aside
Emil: So. That's how it is.
leave emil_toranescu
set emil_dead
Narrator: Pack law has rules, and Kiril keeps them to the letter. A ring of wolves; two men stripping off their shirts; then two wolves, one grey and slow from a month in silver, one black and fresh from the hunt.
Narrator: It is quick, which is the only kind thing about it. Afterwards Kiril stands up a man again, licking his teeth, and nobody in the cave looks at you.
-> kiril_wins

~ betray
set emil_betrayed
Emil [angry]: I misjudged you. That's my fault, not yours. I always was too quick to like people.
leave emil_toranescu
set emil_dead
Narrator: Kiril's favourites take Emil by the arms and walk him back toward the dark. Kiril doesn't watch. He's looking at you, and grinning.
Kiril: Sensible meat. I like sensible meat. The silver's too good for him now. He'll go to the moon at dawn.
-> kiril_wins

~ kiril_wins
set wolf_pack_leader = "kiril"
Narrator: Somewhere back toward the shrine, a woman's voice begins to keen, and keeps on, and then stops all at once, the way a door shuts.
if tarokka.ally.npc == emil_toranescu
quest find_the_ally lost
endif
if guest:ezmerelda
Ezmerelda [angry]: You let that happen. I'll remember who let that happen.
endif
Kiril: Now. Get out of my hills, guests, and give the master my regards.
* The children come with us. -> kids
* We're leaving. -> kids_left

~ kids
Kiril: The pups stay.
* [Persuasion DC 15] Five half-starved children won't make you an army. They'll make you a headache. -> kids_won | kids_refused
* [Intimidation DC 15] Look at us, Kiril. Count us. Then count your wolves. -> kids_won | kids_refused
* [if gold >= 100] (Toss him a purse.) A hundred gold buys a lot of deer. -> kids_bought
* [if gold < 100] We have nothing to trade. -> kids_refused
* Then we'll take them. -> kids_fight

~ kids_won
Kiril: ...Ha. You've got some wolf in you. Fine. Take the pups. They whine all night anyway, and the master can wait for his army till next moon.
-> kids_freed

~ kids_bought
gold -100
set kiril_bribed
Narrator: Kiril weighs the purse in one big hand, then tosses it to the nearest of his wolves without looking.
Kiril: A wolf can be bought. A wolf just can't stay bought. Take the pups before I remember I'm hungry.
-> kids_freed

~ kids_freed
set den_children_freed
quest the_stolen_children freed
Narrator: Somebody unbars the pen. Five children come out holding hands in a line, the eldest at the front, and walk past the wolves with their eyes on the floor and their chins up.
-> kiril_resolve

~ kids_refused
Kiril: No. You've had my generosity. Don't push your luck up my hill.
* Then we'll take them. -> kids_fight
* We're leaving. -> kids_left

~ kids_fight
set pack_challenge_begun
set truce_broken
Kiril [smile]: There it is. I knew there was a wolf in you somewhere.
combat pack_challenge

~ kids_left
set den_children_left
quest the_stolen_children left
Narrator: Behind the pole gate at the back of the den, a girl's voice says something you don't quite catch, and then nothing.
-> kiril_resolve

~ kiril_resolve
set pack_resolved
quest wolves_in_the_hills kiril_leads
if not flag.wolf_den_milestone_reached
set wolf_den_milestone_reached
xp milestone
endif
Kiril: Run along. Tell the valley Kiril Stoyanovich keeps his word. Tell them what else I keep, too.
interject tag:veteran: We walked away from a fight we could have won. I'll be counting that one for a while.
-> END

~ neither
set pack_challenge_begun
leave emil_toranescu
Emil [angry]: You freed me to kill me? Zuleika said you were honest. She was right. You're honest butchers.
Kiril [smile]: Ha! I like these ones. Shame.
interject class:cleric: Wolves that hunt people, and wolves that only hunt deer for now. I won't gamble the next twenty winters on which is which.
combat den_reckoning

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Kiril ruling the den

~ after
if flag.den_children_left and not flag.den_children_freed
Kiril [smile]: Back for the pups? They're getting fat. Not fat enough. Eleven days.
elif flag.kiril_bribed
Kiril [smile]: My favourite customers. Brought another purse? The pups were cheap. Everything else costs more.
else
Kiril: Back again? You're starting to smell like the den. Careful. It sticks.
endif
-> after_menu

~ after_menu
* Why serve the castle? -> after_castle
* [if flag.den_children_left and not flag.den_children_freed] We've changed our minds about the children. -> after_kids
* Goodbye. -> after_bye

~ after_castle
Kiril: Serve? The old man on the hill feeds us and looks the other way. One day he'll look the other way for too long.
interject class:rogue: That's what every dog says about the man with the leash.
Kiril: Mind your tongue, meat. I've a good memory for tongues.
-> after_menu

~ after_kids
Kiril: Have you. Have you, now.
-> kids

~ after_bye
Kiril: Don't come back without a present.
-> END
